---
// The LAN boundary is the whole argument: every box that touches family data
// is inside it, and nothing crosses out.
//
// Solid boxes exist; dashed boxes do not. README.md's hardware table marks the
// Mac Mini, the Pi 4 and the Pi 3 "Running" and the Jetson "Planned". A
// diagram that drew the Jetson as though it were running would misstate it.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 640 296" role="img" aria-labelledby="hc-title hc-desc" class="diagram">
  <title id="hc-title">Home Claw architecture</title>
  <desc id="hc-desc">
    A dashed boundary labelled Home network contains a Mac Mini running local
    inference, two running voice stations drawn with solid outlines, a
    Raspberry Pi 4 and a Raspberry Pi 3, and one planned device drawn with a
    dashed outline: a Jetson Orin Nano bridging to a robot arm. No connection
    crosses the boundary. A legend records that a solid outline means the
    device is running and a dashed outline means it is planned.
  </desc>

  <rect x="8" y="8" width="624" height="244" rx="10" fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor" stroke-dasharray="6 6" opacity="0.45" />
  <text x="24" y="32" font-size="13" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6">HOME NETWORK — nothing leaves</text>

  <!-- Running: solid. -->
  <rect x="232" y="62" width="176" height="66" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" />
  <text x="320" y="86" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">Mac Mini M4 Pro</text>
  <text x="320" y="104" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">local inference · knowledge</text>
  <text x="320" y="120" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">Running</text>

  <!-- Running: solid. -->
  <rect x="30" y="170" width="160" height="66" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" />
  <text x="110" y="194" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">Raspberry Pi 4</text>
  <text x="110" y="212" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">voice · STT · TTS</text>
  <text x="110" y="228" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">Running</text>

  <rect x="240" y="170" width="160" height="66" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" />
  <text x="320" y="194" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">Raspberry Pi 3</text>
  <text x="320" y="212" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">voice · STT · TTS</text>
  <text x="320" y="228" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">Running</text>

  <!-- Planned: dashed. -->

  <rect x="450" y="170" width="160" height="66" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-dasharray="5 4" />
  <text x="530" y="194" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">Jetson Orin Nano</text>
  <text x="530" y="212" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">voice · arm bridge</text>
  <text x="530" y="228" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">Planned</text>

  <!-- Links to running devices are solid. The link to the Jetson is dashed:
       a link to a device that does not exist yet does not exist yet either. -->
  <g stroke="currentColor" opacity="0.55" fill="none">
    <path d="M280 128 L110 170" />
    <path d="M320 128 L320 170" />
  </g>
  <g stroke="currentColor" opacity="0.55" fill="none" stroke-dasharray="5 4">
    <path d="M360 128 L530 170" />
  </g>

  <g class="legend">
    <rect x="8" y="266" width="26" height="16" rx="3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" opacity="0.7" />
    <text x="42" y="279" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">running</text>
    <rect x="140" y="266" width="26" height="16" rx="3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-dasharray="5 4" opacity="0.7" />
    <text x="174" y="279" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">planned — not built</text>
  </g>
</svg>

<style>
  .diagram {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--ink);
    /*
     * Labels are set in SVG user units, so they shrink with the viewBox. At
     * 360px the evidence panel is ~264px wide and this 640-unit drawing
     * scaled to 0.41 — painting 12-unit labels at 5px. Holding the drawing at
     * roughly its own size and letting the panel scroll keeps them at 12px or
     * better everywhere, and stops the diagram ballooning to 24px labels on a
     * wide desktop.
     */
    min-width: 40rem;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
</style>
